    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The investment plan presents a genuinely balanced case for JPM. The bull side highlights a fortress balance sheet ($3.9T assets, $317B equity), market share gains from the 2023 regional banking crisis, and a textbook bullish technical stack (price above all major moving averages, golden cross intact, fresh MACD bullish crossover). However, the bear raises legitimate tactical concerns: RSI at 68.30 approaching overbought, below-average volume (0.93x the 20-day mean) on a 17.5% 60-day advance, and no Q4 2023 earnings data available in the evidence set. At $169.87, the risk-reward is asymmetric \u2014 roughly 3% upside to the near-term target versus 5.3% downside to the 50-day SMA. Given the absence of fundamental confirmation, stretched technicals, and the offsetting strength of both bull and bear cases, maintaining current positioning is the prudent action. A stop-loss below the 10 EMA at $167.28 protects against momentum reversal, while a volume-confirmed breakout above $171 would justify adding.\n\n**Entry Price**: 169.87\n\n**Stop Loss**: 167.28\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain neutral-to-slightly-constructive weight; do not exceed market-weight allocation until either a pullback to the 20-day SMA (~$165.41) improves entry or a volume-confirmed breakout above $171 validates momentum.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
